# PR Verification — Hard Procedural Rule

Never declare a PR "ready to merge" off the back of unit tests + CI alone. Run the full verification battery first.

## Why (this rule has been triggered THREE times)

- **Phase 3 PR #4 round 1:** letterhead missing from rendered HTML (custom Jinja print formats don't auto-wrap with Standard's `{{ letter_head|safe }}`).
- **Phase 3 PR #4 round 2:** no fresh-install smoke, no browser visual check, no PDF round-trip done before declaring green.
- **Phase 4 PR #7:** three Notification templates referenced fields that don't exist on their doctypes (`doc.total_royalty`, `doc.title`, `doc.description`), AND `log_outbound_email` rejected `communication_type='Automated Message'` so every Notification-fired email skipped the audit log. **Fixture-import tests passed because Frappe defers Jinja eval until fire time.**

CI passing means the code compiles and the assertions you happened to write hold — it does **not** mean the feature works.

## The battery (walk it before claiming ready)

1. **Unit tests** — `bench --site SITE run-tests --app myschools` green **locally**, not just on CI.
2. **Lint / pre-commit** — green locally.
3. **Live HTTP smoke** — actually hit the relevant endpoints on the running local site (`http://myschools.localhost:8000`) as Administrator, assert markers in the response. Don't assume `render_template`-style unit tests prove the request path works.
4. **Fresh-install smoke** — `bench drop-site test_mys && bench new-site ... && bench install-app myschools && bench migrate` cleanly, no errors. Catches `after_install` vs `after_sync` / `after_migrate` ordering bugs.
5. **Browser visual check** — open the relevant pages (`/app/<workspace>`, `/printview?...`, `/portal`, etc.) and look at them. Screenshots are cheap.
6. **PDF round-trip** — if a print format ships, generate an actual PDF via `frappe.utils.print_format.download_pdf`. If wkhtmltopdf is broken locally, say so explicitly rather than treating it as "out of scope."
7. **Plan-level verification list** — the plan often lists numbered E2E checks. Walk them, don't skip them.

## Hard procedural rules (because the soft version has failed three times)

- Before pushing the **first commit** on a feature branch, run the full battery locally — not after pushing, not after CI goes green.
- When reporting status to Ali, do not write "ready to merge" (or any synonym) unless you can list, in the same message, the actual battery items run and their results. If not yet run, say *"tests + CI green, still need to run [list]"* — never "ready."
- For Notification/Email Template fixtures specifically, the battery MUST include a Jinja-render-against-real-doc test AND an end-to-end fire smoke (submit a real doc, watch the Communication chain land in `MYS Communication Log`). See [`jinja-render-test`](jinja-render-test.mdc).
- Treat Ali's pushback *"have you tested it?"* as a signal that you shorted the battery — not as a fresh request. Admit the short and run it.

## Sibling rule — verify before STARTING work, not just before merging

Before "kicking off" any phase or starting any plan: `git log --oneline -25` on develop AND `ls` the target directories. **The roadmap may have moved on; the work may already be merged.**

This was already missed once — a `feature/shell-phase-1-2` branch was cut to start Phase 1+2 work that had already shipped in PR #3 (`9ad4351 feat(shell): role-aware ERP shell — brand, workspaces, sidebar scoping`). Don't repeat it.

